This example shows HLS_TOP_TASK with an ap_hs input and an ap_ack output in
Vitis HLS. The task is launched with launch(in, out, c), and the testbench reads
one result per input from the ap_ack output.

Files Included in this Package
==============================
test.h          HLS_TOP_TASK declaration and shared constants
test.cpp        Design (synthesized)
test_tb.cpp     Testbench
hls_config.cfg  Vitis HLS configuration
run_hls.tcl     Tcl flow script
description.json
run.py          Optional Python flow script (vitis -s run.py)
README

Requirements
============
HLS_TOP_TASK requires a Vitis build that provides it (2026.2 or later).

Running the Design (edit run_hls.tcl to set $hls_exec and enable specific run steps)
=========================================================
vitis-run --mode hls --tcl run_hls.tcl

Running the Design using the Python Script
=========================================
vitis -s run.py
